<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parliamentary Republic (Chile)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1891–1925</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Parliamentary Republic was the period of Chilean history from the civil war of 1891 to the Constitution of 1925, during which Congress dominated weak presidents and cabinets changed frequently. Financed by nitrate exports, the oligarchic governments of the time did little to address the 'social question' of urban and mining workers, and the period ended amid military intervention in 1924–1925.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/parliamentary-republic-chile.jpg" alt="Parliamentary Republic (Chile)" width="320" height="178" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James2813, modified from File:Flag of Chile (Rectangular canton variant 2).svg · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Chile_(1818%E2%80%931912).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
